 "notes": "FACTS CHECKED (with source)\n- Founded 2010 (New York) by Adam Neumann and Miguel McKelvey; $47B valuation Jan 2019 (Wikipedia; Fox Business)\n- 2018: revenue $1.82B, net loss $1.6B; lease obligations $17.9B; Class B/C shares 20 votes vs 1 (The Motley Fool, S-1 coverage, Aug 14, 2019)\n- $5.9M paid to Neumann for the 'We' trademark, returned after backlash (Fox Business; Inc.)\n- Related-party leases in buildings Neumann had stakes in (disclosed in the S-1)\n- Neumann out as CEO Sep 24, 2019; IPO withdrawn Sep 30, 2019 (Wikipedia)\n- SoftBank takeover at ~$8B; Neumann deal up to $1.7B: ~$1B share purchase, $500M credit line, $185M consulting (TechCrunch, Oct 22, 2019, citing WSJ)\n- SPAC (BowX) listing Oct 2021 at ~$9B (REBusiness); never profitable (Fox Business)\n- Chapter 11 Nov 2023 (NJ); market cap ~$21M Dec 2023 (Wikipedia)\n- Exit from bankruptcy Jun 11, 2024; Yardi majority owner; $4B+ debt cut; ~170 locations exited (Newser, Jun 13, 2024)\n- a16z $350M into Flow, largest single check ever (TechCrunch, Aug 15, 2022)\n- ~2,400 layoffs announced Nov 21, 2019 (CNN); expected valuation reported at ~$10B in Sep 2019 (Wikipedia)\n- REVIEW: preview (titles, covers, voice) approved by Vinícius on 16/10/2026"
